<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Alliance Pharmaceuticals hikes H1 earnings.</title>
<headline>Alliance Pharmaceuticals hikes H1 earnings.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Aug 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     5.2	   vs 1.3</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   3.12	  vs 0.77</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   3.14	  vs 0.96</p>
<p>    Tax			  -	    vs  -</p>
<p>    Attrib to minorities  0.11	  vs 0.19</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.76	  vs 0.81</p>
<p>    Turnover		  38.11	 vs 28.64</p>
<p>Full name: Alliance Pharamceuticals Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said its policy was to distribute 25 percent of earnings in semi-annual dividends. The first dividend will be declared next May out of profits for the full year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
